          "title": "A division of labour, inherited",
          "text": "The world economy is organised into a centre that makes manufactures and a periphery that supplies primary commodities. The division is not natural or chosen; for most of the periphery it was established under colonial rule and survived independence intact, because the ports, railways and firms built to move commodities outward were still there.",
