          "title": "Demand grows unevenly",
          "text": "As world incomes rise, spending shifts towards manufactures and services and away from food and raw materials in proportional terms. Engel's law at the level of a whole economy. Demand for what the periphery sells therefore grows more slowly than demand for what it buys, which pushes on the relative price year after year.",
