          "title": "The surplus travels upward",
          "text": "Frank's addition. The relation repeats at every scale: a metropolis extracts from its satellites, and each satellite is itself a metropolis for those below it. A landless labourer supplies a landlord, who supplies a provincial trader, who supplies a national capital, which supplies a world centre. Development at one node is not held back by isolation from this chain but produced by position within it, which is why the periphery's brief episodes of growth tend to come when the chain is broken by war or depression.",
