          "title": "And one number decides the future",
          "text": "Lambda-k is the share of new investment directed into the capital goods department. It is a policy choice, not a market outcome. A high lambda-k means fewer consumer goods this decade and a faster rate of growth of investment itself, which compounds. Mahalanobis showed that in the long run this share, rather than the overall saving rate, governs where the growth path ends up.",
